# PSR-6c1 — SDK async durable smoke port

## Intent

Unblock Harbor durable wiring without forcing a Denali clone: evolve
`createWorkspaceGuestSmokeHttpHandlers` so a later host-backed port can be
**async** and can serve a **non-501 default path** when durable mode is on.

## Changes

| API | Behavior |
| --- | --- |
| `WorkspaceGuestSmokeCatalogPort` | `listPublished` / `getPublished` / `createRegistration` may return `T` or `Promise<T>` |
| `isDurableEnabled?: () => boolean` | When true (and seed false), surface is allowed — **no** 501 |
| Durable + no `catalogPort` | Empty list / 404 detail / register not-found — **not** fixture `buildCard` fallback |
| Seed path | Unchanged for guest-club / Harbor memory store (sync port still valid) |

## Non-goals

- Wiring Harbor HTTP to durable mode (`isDurableEnabled` stays unused there)
- API `configureHarbor*` host
- Prisma adapters
- Recert / tier promote

## Verify

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-6c1-sdk-async-durable-port-smoke.mjs
pnpm --filter @app-tour/workspace-sdk exec node --import tsx --test test/http-plib-dg1.spec.ts
```

